# Boundary PMTiles are build output of scripts/build-boundary-tiles.py.
# Ignored while the pipeline is being validated: the archives are large
# binaries and a half-written one (note the *-journal files tippecanoe
# leaves mid-run) must never reach a commit. Whether the finished tiles
# get committed or fetched at deploy time is still an open decision —
# the repo is already 192 MB and contributor clone weight is on the
# roadmap, so the answer depends on their final size.

# Boundary PMTiles: six levels ship in-repo. village.pmtiles (267 MB) does
# not — GitHub rejects files over 100 MB. Rebuild it with
# scripts/build-boundary-tiles.py village.
data/tiles/village.pmtiles

# The national land-surface-temperature mosaic (518 MB) is an intermediate,
# not a shipped asset: nothing in the site reads it. It exists so the zonal
# pass in scripts/build-boundary-heat.py can stamp a heat value onto boundary
# polygons, and those values ship inside the PMTiles archives instead.
# Rebuild with scripts/build-lst-mosaic.py — about 20 minutes.
data/rasters/
